{"title": "The price of your Android XR glasses can quickly skyrocket with add-ons", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/android-xr-glasses-add-on-prices/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/android-xr-intelligent-eyewear-warby-parker-29.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Google’s first collection of Intelligent Eyewear has arrived and, <em>oh boy</em>, the prices are not cheap. While this first batch starts at $395, you’ll be paying a fair bit more for a pair of Android XR glasses if you need to add anything on. Here’s a quick overview.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/android-xr-glasses-add-on-prices/#more-737061\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T07:45:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Pixel Watch and Fitbit Air will be able to control Android XR glasses with gestures", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/android-xr-will-support-piel-watch-and-fitbit-air-control/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/android-xr-intelligent-eyewear-warby-parker-28.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Android XR glasses get their own control wearable, but you might already own it. Google says the Fitbit Air and Pixel Watch will be able to control Android XR glasses.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/android-xr-will-support-piel-watch-and-fitbit-air-control/#more-737086\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T07:39:04+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "‘Hey Gemini’ hotword debuts on Android XR glasses", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/hey-gemini-hotword-debuts-on-android-xr-glasses/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/android-xr-intelligent-eyewear-warby-parker-37.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Google is finally introducing a “Hey Gemini” hotword for its AI assistant, but it’s only on Android XR glasses to start.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/hey-gemini-hotword-debuts-on-android-xr-glasses/#more-736760\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T06:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Here’s how Google’s Android XR glasses are handling the camera & privacy", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-android-xr-glasses-camera-privacy/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/android-xr-intelligent-eyewear-gentle-monster-19.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Google’s Intelligent Eyewear push with the first Android XR glasses from Warby Parker and Gentle Monster are forced into an unfortunate uphill battle. The “perv glasses” stigma is very real because, frankly, early movers in this category didn’t respect privacy. Here’s how Android XR and Gemini are handling the camera and privacy on “Intelligent Eyewear,” and why I think Google has struck a near-perfect balance.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-android-xr-glasses-camera-privacy/#more-736482\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T05:15:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Google’s new Android XR glasses work with iOS, Made for iPhone certified", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-glasses-iphone-support/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/android-xr-intelligent-eyewear-warby-parker-34.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Google today <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/?p=736529\">announced</a> Android XR audio glasses called Intelligent Eyewear that notably support iOS with Made for iPhone certification.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-glasses-iphone-support/#more-736979\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T05:05:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Google launches Intelligent Eyewear glasses: $395+, pre-order today, ships Dec. 10", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-intelligent-eyewear-glasses/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/android-xr-intelligent-eyewear-warby-parker-9.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">After years of development, Google is launching its second foray into smart glasses with Intelligent Eyewear that supports Android and iOS. Pre-orders start today at <a href=\"https://www.gentlemonster.com/us/en/category/intelligent-eyewear/shop-all\">Gentle Monster</a> and <a href=\"https://www.warbyparker.com/collections/intelligent-eyewear\">Warby Parker</a>, with the audio glasses shipping on December 10.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-intelligent-eyewear-glasses/#more-736529\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T05:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Disney just launched 3D movies on the Meta Quest ahead of Meta VR Glasses’ release", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/disney-just-launched-3d-movies-on-the-meta-quest-ahead-of-meta-vr-glasses-release/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/monsters-inc-scare-floor-meta-quest-3d.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All available 3D movies are included with your Disney+ subscription and come with extras you can only experience in VR.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/disney-just-launched-3d-movies-on-the-meta-quest-ahead-of-meta-vr-glasses-release/#more-737025\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T04:50:57+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "The iPhone Duo’s rocky launch is a reminder of how far Android foldables have come", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/the-iphone-duos-rocky-launch-is-a-reminder-of-how-far-android-foldables-have-come/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/galaxy-z-fold-8-iphone-duo-4.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Good morning. Today I’m <a href=\"https://opensource.builders/\">finding open source alternatives to all of my apps</a>, poring through Pitchfork’s list of the <a href=\"https://pitchfork.com/story/the-100-best-indie-rock-albums-of-all-time/\">100 best indie rock albums</a> to find ones I haven’t listened to, and preparing my body for November 19th by <a href=\"https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/89834o94713o21/pre-load-grand-theft-auto-vi-now\">pre-loading GTA VI</a> (and replaying <a href=\"https://www.rockstargames.com/games/IV\">GTA IV</a> in the meantime). </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Inbox</em> is the tech newsletter that goes beyond the news cycle. We cover the most important 9to5Google stories from the last couple of days along with a few highlights from around the web. We publish every Tuesday and Thursday, and if you like what you read, <a href=\"https://9to5google.beehiiv.com/subscribe\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">please subscribe</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/the-iphone-duos-rocky-launch-is-a-reminder-of-how-far-android-foldables-have-come/#more-736873\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-12T03:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "The Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 5 would be my perfect Steam tablet if it didn’t cost $900", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/11/lenovo-legion-tab-gen-5-review/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/lenovo-legion-tab-gen-5-revview-13.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For every Android-powered slate I’ve used, only Nvidia’s Shield Tablet really stands out in my memory. Part of the company’s occasional (<a href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/10/02/nvidia-shield-tv-pro-price-hike/\">and all-but-dead</a>) dip into hardware products, the Shield Tablet — and its revitalized K1 follow-up, which I also owned through a recall program on the original — carried me through the back half of college, frequently keeping my Chromebook in my backpack in lieu of a mini Bluetooth keyboard or the Shield Tablet’s built-in stylus. Its front-firing speakers made it great for movie-watching, and while I’m not much of a mobile gamer, I did find it to be a great device for emulation, especially when paired with an external controller.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/11/lenovo-legion-tab-gen-5-review/#more-736069\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-11T11:30:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-16T20:12:00.919170+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
